{"repositoryId":1089388346,"availability":"available","full":"leaningtech/browserpod-meta","name":"browserpod-meta","description":"A browser-native code sandbox. Run Node.js, Rust, C++, Python (preview), and other full-stack runtimes directly in the browser. ","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":222,"forks":14,"created":"2025-11-04T09:22:55Z","updated":"2026-10-07T10:17:10Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://browserpod.io","topics":["api","architecture","browser","client-side","editor","infrastructure","nodejs","runtime","runtime-execution","sandbox"],"demo":"https://v6.yarnpkg.com/playground","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T18:03:49.875Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T18:03:49.875Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T18:03:49.875Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T18:03:49.875Z","stars":222,"forks":14}],"technologies":["Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["BrowserPod is a WebAssembly-based API that creates a lightweight Linux virtual machine directly in a user's browser tab. Its in-browser Linux-like kernel supports sandboxed runtime environments including Node.js, Rust and Python (preview), with more coming soon.","Developers use BrowserPod to sandbox untrusted and AI-generated code in the browser, build web applications that embed server-side processes client-side, create interactive documentation and playgrounds and run AI coding CLIs in-browser without modification (e.g., Claude Code, Codex)."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/leaningtech/browserpod-meta/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"fcd53e03d59226adda3ae1502ef3c7082dd005b2128faa6b3472f6c125c386b6","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T18:03:50.007Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T18:03:50.007Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"BrowserPod is a WebAssembly-based API that creates a lightweight Linux virtual machine directly in a user's browser tab. Its in-browser Linux-like kernel supports sandbox